@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+# Timed-out job retries: complete
+
+All three public entry points now retry `failed` and `timed_out` jobs with the
+same behavior. Their `retry(store, job_id) -> Job` signatures remain usable,
+including keyword arguments.
+
+## Changes and decision
+
+- `jobqueue/retry.py` owns lookup, eligibility, the attempt limit, updating the
+  immutable job and saving it. `api.py`, `cli.py` and `scheduler.py` re-export it.
+- Updating each copy would work, but would leave three owners of one policy.
+  The shared operation removes that existing duplication with no forwarding
+  functions or new configuration. The original suite passed after extraction,
+  before the eligibility change.
+- `tests/test_retry.py` exercises every entry point with real `Job` and `Store`
+  instances: both eligible states, success at attempts 0–2, rejection at 3 and
+  above, missing jobs, ineligible-state precedence and failed saves. Rejection
+  tests make saving unavailable so an accidental save cannot pass unnoticed.
+  Save-failure checks cover both zero and one previous successful write.
+- `README.md` records the new accepted states and shared implementation. The
+  legacy `job is not failed` message and validation order remain intentional.
+
+## Evidence
+
+Run from this project:
+
+```sh
+python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests -v
+```
+
+- Original baseline: `Ran 3 tests in 0.001s` / `OK`.
+- Shared-operation extraction, before behavior change: `Ran 3 tests in 0.002s`
+  / `OK`.
+- Expanded tests before enabling `timed_out`: `FAILED (failures=6, errors=15)`;
+  failures were the newly requested timed-out cases.
+- Final result: `Ran 5 tests in 0.002s` / `OK`.
+
+A separate standard-library `inspect.signature` check confirmed both parameter
+names, their positional/keyword calling convention, annotations and return type.
+Keyword calls succeeded through all three entry points. Final source inspection
+found one retry implementation and all three consumers using it.
+
+## Remaining work and limits
+
+None for the requested behavior. No separate build or lint tooling is configured.
+No dependency, persistence or concurrency mechanism was added.
+
+## Guidance used
+
+- Supplied `coder.md` role guidance.
+- Supplied `software-engineering.md` practitioner guidance.
